cff-version: 1.2.0
message: >-
  If you use TAUT, or build on the concepts it implements —
  workspace-as-a-build-artifact distribution of AI-agent toolchains
  under a lock file and a fail-closed integrity gate — please cite it
  as below.
title: "TAUT — Toolchain Actualization Under Trust"
type: software
authors:
  - given-names: Yuriy
    family-names: Orlov
    email: yuriy.orlov@undertrust.dev
abstract: >-
  TAUT is a distribution engine for AI-agent toolchains. It compiles a
  harness-neutral data pack (skills, subagents, guidelines, an MCP
  catalog) into per-harness agent workspaces (Claude Code, Codex,
  opencode), pins the engine and pack versions plus a sha256 checksum
  for every installed artifact in a lock file, and enforces integrity
  at runtime with a fail-closed gate. Nobody edits the workspace: the
  pack is the single reviewed source, and the workspace is a build
  artifact.
keywords:
  - ai-agents
  - agentic-coding
  - llm-toolchain
  - workspace-as-build-artifact
  - toolchain-distribution
  - integrity-gate
  - lockfile
  - supply-chain
  - claude-code
  - codex
  - opencode
repository-code: "https://github.com/yurgeno/taut"
license: Apache-2.0
version: 0.8.0
date-released: '2026-10-22'
